<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gerald Templer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1898">1898</a>–<a href="/years/1979">1979</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gerald Templer was a British army officer who served as High Commissioner in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malaya">Malaya</a> from 1952 to 1954 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malayan-emergency">Malayan Emergency</a>. Combining civil and military command, he pressed on with the resettlement of rural Chinese into new villages, strict food control and a campaign to win the hearts and minds of the population, which greatly weakened the communist insurgents. He later became a field marshal and Chief of the Imperial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-general-staff">General Staff</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gerald-templer.jpg" alt="Gerald Templer" width="162" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Malayan Information Centre · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_gerald_templer.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
